From 74137225165f4dd05ed2808ac198c9c9795e4292 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Phase1 Draft (Claude, for Terhi review)" <draft@local>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 05:06:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] fix(model+sim): MODEL SEMANTICS CHANGE, gated on sign-off
 -- the spatial trigger is now a REAL-unit object: offspring displacements are
 N(0, sigmax_2 * I) in the units of the input X/Y columns, isotropic
 regardless of the bounding rectangle's shape. Previously the kernel was
 isotropic in INTERNAL (unit-square) coordinates, so the real-space kernel was
 an axis-aligned anisotropic Gaussian whose anisotropy ratio equaled the
 bounding box's aspect ratio -- the fitted kernel FAMILY was a function of a
 preprocessing choice (consolidation doc, Prop. "aniso"), and per-park
 bounding boxes implied per-park kernel geometries. THIS CHANGES THE FITTED
 MODEL AND THE MEANING OF sigmax_2 (now squared REAL units; priors must be
 restated; posteriors become directly interpretable and comparable across
 domains). All three legs move in ONE commit because simulation-inference
 symmetry cannot survive a split: (1) event term routes through new atom
 real_spatial_trigger_values -- internal displacements stretched per axis,
 real-area density evaluated, then the Jacobian sx*sy converts the density to
 the internal measure the likelihood integrates over (the review-caught unit
 issue: phi_real is per REAL area, mu is per INTERNAL area; the Jacobian is
 the single point where they reconcile); (2) the compensator's erf limits
 become REAL distances to the rectangle edges (axis_scales is a REQUIRED
 keyword-only arg -- unit interfaces are declared, never implicit; the mass is
 dimensionless so no Jacobian appears); (3) _sim_offspring's spatial draw is
 real-unit directly (the internal-draw * box-span rescale is deleted -- that
 rescale WAS the defect). On a square box of side L, sigma_real = sigma_int *
 L reproduces the old kernel EXACTLY (Jacobian L^2 cancels the density
 normalization) -- pinned as an algebraic special case. (I10) is RESTATED, a
 signed-off test edit: unit invariance becomes unit COVARIANCE (similarity
 transformations with sigmax_2 -> c^2 sigmax_2), and the OLD identity --
 fixed-parameter invariance under non-uniform axis rescaling -- is now
 asserted to FAIL (negative control; that invariance was the defect). New
 regression, verified RED pre-fix: on a 4:1 box the cascade's per-axis real
 variance ratio was 16.97 (predicted (Lx/Ly)^2 = 16), post-fix ~1. New atom +
 nonsquare-compensator tests against float64 references. Verified: 43/43;
 value+gradient pins BIT-IDENTICAL on every unit-box config (hawkes,
 cox_hawkes, lgcp) -- the L=1 special case is exact multiplication by 1.0f --
 and moved ONLY on the non-square 4:1 pin config (worst rel move 0.96 on
 d_sigmax_2), which is the fix's signature, recorded not promised. ruff clean.

